Perturbations, normal modes and what linear stability proves (@fd-stability: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA", #source "../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P", #source "../sources/CFD-Verification-and-Validation-NPARC.lingua#r_7P72ZWZEJ0SVMWFDGK52N9AZPV", #fluid-dynamics "Transition-disturbance-amplitude-and-transient-growth.lingua#r_3YVWXR0JBV81JE1W6E58FB6F6A") { r_48XANNJ6W3VYE8XSV9358W16AW
**Read:** [Fluid Mechanics — David Tong](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA), chapter 5 shear-flow stability and necessary conditions; [Advanced fluid dynamics — Mei notes and MIT modules](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P), chapter 5 inviscid and viscous parallel-flow instability; [CFD verification and validation — NPARC Alliance](../sources/CFD-Verification-and-Validation-NPARC.lingua#r_7P72ZWZEJ0SVMWFDGK52N9AZPV), consistency and convergence methods.

Specify a base flow that satisfies its own equations and boundary conditions, then introduce a small perturbation. Linearization retains terms first order in its amplitude. A modal ansatz converts an initial-value question into an eigenvalue problem only under the stated temporal and spatial structure. A positive growth rate proves growth of that linear mode, not the amplitude or statistics of the later nonlinear state.

Distinguish temporal growth at real wavenumber from spatial amplification at real frequency, and convective from absolute instability. In a parallel inviscid shear flow, derive the Rayleigh equation and its inflection-point necessary condition under its assumptions. For viscous parallel flow, follow the Orr–Sommerfeld formulation, including all boundary conditions and nondimensionalization.

Check a computed eigenmode against residual, grid/order changes and an independent time evolution of a small disturbance. Boundary truncation and spurious eigenvalues can create convincing false growth. A necessary condition is not sufficient, and decay of every individual mode does not rule out transient amplification in a non-normal linear system.

**Continue:** [Transition, disturbance amplitude and transient growth](Transition-disturbance-amplitude-and-transient-growth.lingua#r_3YVWXR0JBV81JE1W6E58FB6F6A).

